<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kamianets-Podilskyi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kamieniec Podolski, Kamenets-Podolsky</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kamianets-Podilskyi is a city in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, in the historical region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/podolia">Podolia</a>, built on a rocky island in a loop of the Smotrych river. Its castle, strengthened by the Koriatovich princes in the 14th century and later by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Polish crown</a>, made it the chief stronghold of Podolia. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> held it from 1672 to 1699.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kamianets-podilskyi.jpg" alt="Kamianets-Podilskyi" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Grzegorz Gołębiowski · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zamek_w_Kamie%C5%84cu_Podolskim_2019.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
